    <heading level="1">Graphical</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, rotate through the given angle based on the given equation. Give the new equation and graph the original and rotated equation.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="31" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y = - x^{2},\theta = - 45^{\circ}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 2 ( x ′ + y ′ )= 1 2 ( x ′ - y ′ ) 2 2 2 ( x ′ + y ′ )= 1 2 ( x ′ - y ′ ) 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="32" has_solution="false">
